\section{Formal Physics Module Specification}
\subsection{Ball Flight Dynamics (Aero-Ballistics)}
We model the batted-ball trajectory under gravity, drag, and Magnus lift:
\begin{equation}
m \frac{d\mathbf{v}}{dt}
= m \mathbf{g}
- \frac{1}{2} \rho_{\text{air}} C_d A \|\mathbf{v}\| \mathbf{v}
+ \frac{1}{2} \rho_{\text{air}} C_l A \|\mathbf{v}\|^2 \hat{\mathbf{L}}(\boldsymbol{\omega}, \mathbf{v}),
\end{equation}
where \(m\) is the ball mass, \(\mathbf{v}\) velocity, \(\rho_{\text{air}}\) air density,
\(C_d\) drag coefficient, \(C_l\) lift coefficient, \(A\) cross-sectional area,
and \(\boldsymbol{\omega}\) the spin vector.

\subsection{Bat--Ball Collision Mechanics}
We model impact via an impulse-momentum formulation with a dynamic coefficient of restitution:
\begin{equation}
\mathbf{J}
= m_{\text{eff}} (1 + e_{\text{COR}}) (\mathbf{v}_{\text{bat}} - \mathbf{v}_{\text{ball}}),
\end{equation}
where \(m_{\text{eff}}\) is the effective mass, \(e_{\text{COR}}\) depends on bat
material and impact location, and \(\mathbf{v}_{\text{bat}}, \mathbf{v}_{\text{ball}}\)
are pre-impact velocities.

